exports[`Fixture Snapshots > snapshot: ELBOW-left-early-3tx 1`] = `
"Subjective
Follow up visit
Patient reports: there is improvement of symptom(s) because of can move joint more freely and with less pain .
Patient still c/o Dull, Aching pain on elbow without radiation, associated with muscles soreness (scale as 60%), impaired performing ADL's with mild to moderate difficulty of long hours of driving .

Pain Scale: 5-4 /10
Pain frequency: Frequent (symptoms occur between 51% and 75% of the time)

Objective
Muscles Testing:
Tightness muscles noted along Lattisimus dorsi, Internal oblique, External oblique
Grading Scale: Mild to moderate

Tenderness muscle noted along Erector spinae, Hamstrings, Gluteus Maximus

Grading Scale: (+1)= There is mild tenderness to palpation

Muscles spasm noted along External oblique, Erector spinae, Hamstrings
Frequency Grading Scale:(+1)=No spontaneous spasms; vigorous sensory and motor stimulation results in spasms.

Left Elbow Muscles Strength and Joint ROM
5/5 Flexion: 130 degree (normal)
5/5 Extension: 10 degree (normal)
4+/5 Left side flexion: 60 degree (normal)
5/5 Rt side flexion: 60 degree (normal)
5/5 Left side rotation: 60 degree (normal)
4+/5 Right side rotation: 60 degree (normal)

Inspection: weak muscles and dry skin without luster

tongue
thin white coat
pulse
string-taut

Assessment
The patient continues treatment for elbow area today.
The patient's general condition is good, compared with last treatment, the patient presents with improvement of symptom(s). The patient has decreased pain frequency and muscles soreness sensation, physical finding has reduced joint ROM limitation, local muscles tenderness and local muscles spasms and increased muscles strength. Patient tolerated treatment with excellent outcome due reducing pain. No adverse side effect post treatment.
Current patient still has Qi Stagnation in local meridian that cause the pain.

Plan
Today's treatment principles:
continue to be emphasize on moving qi to speed up the recovery, soothe the tendon.

Select Needle Size :36#x0.5" , 34#x1" ,30# x1.5"
Daily acupuncture treatment for elbow - Personal one on one contact with the patient (Total Operation Time: 15 mins)

Front Points: (15 mins) - personal one on one contact with the patient
1. Greeting patient, Review of the chart, Routine examination of the patient current condition, washing hands, setting up the clean field, selecting acupuncture needle size, selecting location, marking and cleaning the points, Initial Acupuncture needle inserted without electrical stimulation HT3, LU5, LI10, LI11

Removing and properly disposing of needles
Post treatment service and education patient about precautions at home after treatment.
Documentation
---VISIT---
Subjective
Follow up visit
Patient reports: there is improvement of symptom(s) because of reduced joint stiffness and swelling .
Patient still c/o Dull, Aching pain on elbow without radiation, associated with muscles soreness (scale as 50%), impaired performing ADL's with mild difficulty of long hours of driving .

Pain Scale: 4-3 /10
Pain frequency: Frequent (symptoms occur between 51% and 75% of the time)

Objective
Muscles Testing:
Tightness muscles noted along Lattisimus dorsi, Internal oblique, External oblique
Grading Scale: Mild to moderate

Tenderness muscle noted along Erector spinae, Hamstrings, Gluteus Maximus

Grading Scale: (+1)= There is mild tenderness to palpation

Muscles spasm noted along External oblique, Erector spinae, Hamstrings
Frequency Grading Scale:(+1)=No spontaneous spasms; vigorous sensory and motor stimulation results in spasms.

Left Elbow Muscles Strength and Joint ROM
5/5 Flexion: 130 degree (normal)
5/5 Extension: 10 degree (normal)
5/5 Left side flexion: 60 degree (normal)
5/5 Rt side flexion: 65 degree (normal)
5/5 Left side rotation: 60 degree (normal)
5/5 Right side rotation: 60 degree (normal)

Inspection: weak muscles and dry skin without luster

tongue
thin white coat
pulse
string-taut

Assessment
The patient continues treatment for elbow area today.
The patient's general condition is good, compared with last treatment, the patient presents with improvement of symptom(s). The patient has decreased pain, muscles soreness sensation and muscles stiffness sensation, physical finding has reduced joint ROM limitation and increased muscles strength. Patient tolerated acupuncture session with good outcome in improving ROM. No adverse side effect post treatment.
Current patient still has Qi Stagnation in local meridian that cause the pain.

